<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Standard takes full control of Uganda bank.</title>
<headline>Standard takes full control of Uganda bank.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's Standard Bank Investment Corp Ltd said on Tuesday it had bought the Ugandan government's 49 percent shareholding in Stanbic Bank Uganda Ltd in a US$6.5 million deal.  </p>
<p>&quot;We are delighted to have concluded this deal with the Ugandan government. It demonstrates our confidence in the economic stability of Uganda,&quot; said Graeme Bell, senior general manager, African Banking Group.</p>
<p>Bell said President Yoweri Museveni's government had created a stable investment climate in the country.</p>
</text>
